Provenance: UNetFormer decoder adapted from
https://github.com/WangLibo1995/GeoSeg
("UNetFormer: A UNet-like transformer for efficient semantic segmentation of
remote sensing urban scene imagery", ISPRS Journal 2022)

The upstream GeoSeg repository is licensed **GPL-3.0** (GitHub license badge;
full text in `GPL-3.0.LICENSE`, fetched from the upstream repository's own
LICENSE file).

Consequence for this distribution: the UNetFormer decoder code carries the
GPL-3.0 terms. GPL-3.0 permits commercial use BUT is copy-left: if you
distribute a work that includes this component, that distribution must be
licensed under GPL-3.0 (or a compatible license) and must provide source.
This is one of the reasons the repository as a whole is positioned as a
RESEARCH distribution — see NOTICE and README ("License").
